  "name": "meeting-minutes",
  "description": "A historical archive documenting the technical evolution and governance of the Rust programming language from 2011 to 2014. It contains detailed records of weekly planning meetings, RFC triage, and API reviews that shaped core features such as the ownership model, lifetime elision, and concurrency semantics. This repository serves as a primary record of the design decisions leading up to the Rust 1.0 stabilization.",
